      },
      "text": " I think the biggest issue is that most people don't know what they use,"
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:02,720",
        "to": "00:00:06,320"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 2720,
        "to": 6320
      },
      "text": " because if you install a package, it can include additional packages."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:06,320",
        "to": "00:00:11,200"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 6320,
        "to": 11200
      },
      "text": " You install a package and then it's a dependency of someone else, so you can't even track it."
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:11,200",
        "to": "00:00:15,520"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 11200,
        "to": 15520
      },
      "text": " Even if you then just redeploy your project because you did a small update"
    },
    {
      "timestamps": {
        "from": "00:00:16,080",
        "to": "00:00:20,240"
      },
      "offsets": {
        "from": 16080,
        "to": 20240
      },
      "text": " on something that doesn't impact anything, it reinstalls all the packages"
